/tmp/arxiv2512.17821.KJyVUD/src/Pratt_CubesFromProducts.tex:200:Let $a,b,c$ be nonzero integers, and let $D$ denote the cube-free part of $abc$. If $D \in \mathcal{L}$, then the equation $ax^3+by^3+cz^3=0$ has no solutions in nonzero integers $x,y,z$.
